---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"OCD Treatment in Provo & Utah County | Tangible Therapy"} description={"OCD treatment in Provo, Orem, & Sandy using ERP; the gold-standard approach. Break free from obsessions and compulsions. Book a free 15-minute consult."}>
<section class="sec t-bright h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-29-f6346a.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:50% 50%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.4"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:9">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/5/21;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">OCD Therapy in Utah</h1><p class="ta-center">Break free from obsessive thoughts and compulsive patterns with tools that work</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/11/8/17;--m:7/4/9/8;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Book Your First Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/13/26;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/trigger-1-4d292e.png" alt="Diagram of the Tangible Therapy OCD and Anxiety Cycle with segments labeled Trigger, Intrusive/Obsessive Thoughts, Fear Forecast, Intolerable Emotion, Safety Behaviors, Decreased Tolerance, illustrating a cycle with colored segments." width="3456" height="4608" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/6/12;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Understand what’s really happening</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/12/12;--m:4/2/12/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Living with OCD means feeling trapped in a loop with obsessive thoughts that won’t quiet down and rituals that seem impossible to resist. These patterns aren’t quirks or habits. They’re symptoms of a treatable condition.</p><p>At Tangible Therapy, we help you understand what OCD is, how it works, and what you can do to take control.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/12/13;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-33-b74a9f.jpg" alt="a female OCD therapist in a light shirt at Tangible Therapy in Provo, Utah. Smiling and sitting across from a man in a brown shirt while they do ERP Therapy." width="2439" height="1932" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/15/6/25;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>A safe space to talk without shame</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/15/13/25;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>OCD may make you feel isolated or ashamed of your thoughts, even when you know they don’t make sense. But you’re not broken, and you’re not alone. We offer a judgment-free space where you can talk openly about your fears, behaviors, and daily struggles.</p><p>No topic is too small, too strange, or too hard to bring into the room.<br/></p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/13/26;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-61-b2ce79.jpg" alt="a female OCD therapist in a light shirt at Tangible Therapy in Orem, Utah. Smiling and sitting across from a woman in a brown shirt" width="3300" height="2550" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/6/12;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Proven tools to break the cycle</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/11/12;--m:4/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>We use evidence-based therapies like Exposure and Response Prevention (ERP), which is considered the gold standard for treating OCD. This method helps you gradually face your fears without giving in to compulsions. It also gives you back a sense of control.</p><p>You'll learn how to respond differently to obsessive thoughts and reduce the anxiety they create, one step at a time.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:11;--mrows:17">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/2/11/13;--m:9/2/16/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/unsplash-image-m6gy9ohgii-0d2353.jpg" alt="A young man with OCD sitting on a ledge with a circular window behind him, showing a city skyline and clear blue sky." width="2000" height="2500" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/4/24;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Support built for your life</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/15/9/24;--m:3/2/10/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>OCD shows up in all kinds of ways: rituals, intrusive thoughts, constant checking, relationships, or mental compulsions. No matter how it looks to you, we tailor treatment to your experience. Together, we’ll create a plan that helps you move forward with confidence and clarity.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:9/15/11/21;--m:16/3/18/9;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Book Your Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:5;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/6/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">OCD Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/6/6/22;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/ocd" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:6.6vmax;padding-bottom:6.6vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>50 minutes focused on breaking patterns and building resilience</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A stronger, healthier relationship with your thoughts and reactions</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Targeted, evidence-based guidance for the specific ways OCD shows up in your life</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Practical tools rooted in expertise to help you resist compulsions and reduce anxiety</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A calm, supportive space where you can face fears without judgment</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Clear insight into how OCD functions — and how you can take back control</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What is OCD, really?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (OCD) is more than liking things neat or organized. It involves intrusive, unwanted thoughts (obsessions) and repetitive behaviors or mental rituals (compulsions) done to relieve anxiety. OCD can take many forms, and it’s treatable with the right approach.</p></div></details><details><summary>How do I know if I have OCD?</summary><div class="rte"><p>If you feel trapped in thought loops or find yourself repeating actions to feel right, you might be experiencing symptoms of OCD. A trained therapist can help you understand what’s going on and give you a clear diagnosis if needed.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will therapy force me to face all my fears at once?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. ERP is structured and collaborative. We go at your pace, with your input. You’ll never be pushed into anything before you’re ready. The goal is to build confidence step by step, not overwhelm you.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/11/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Is OCD therapy different from regular counseling?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes. OCD requires a more targeted, skills-based approach. While emotional support is part of the process, we focus heavily on specific techniques to reduce compulsions and challenge obsessive thought patterns.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if my OCD symptoms are really personal or disturbing?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s completely normal. OCD often targets the things you care about most. We’ve heard it all, and we never judge. You’re not your thoughts — and you don’t have to carry them alone.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
